  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field associated with a light wave is given by <math><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1.57</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math> (where <math><mi>x</mi></math> and <math><mi>t</mi></math> are in metre and second respectively). The stopping potential when this light is used in an experiment on photoelectric effect with the emitter having work function <math><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.9</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>e</mn><mn>V</mn></math> is.",
